<title>INDIA: India Finolex Cables 96/97 net falls.</title>
<headline>India Finolex Cables 96/97 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	   (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		483.8     vs	551.0</p>
<p>    Sales		   4,640.0     vs    4,876.6</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)	  26.8     vs	 30.5</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	   5.5     vs	  5.5</p>
<p>    Other income	    165.7     vs	263.9</p>
<p>    Expenditure	   3,736.5     vs    3,969.1</p>
<p>    Interest		  213.5     vs	221.0</p>
<p>    Gross profit	    855.7     vs	950.4</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    151.9     vs	124.7</p>
<p>    Tax			 220.0     vs	274.7</p>
<p>Note - Finolex Cables Ltd managing director G.S. Talauliker said that operations were hit by &quot;inordinate delay in finalising orders&quot; by the government's Department of Telecommunication.</p>
<p>&quot;Company is in the process of reducing its dependence on Government orders by increasing its reliance on the market by higher production of light duty cables and power cables,&quot; he said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
</text>
